# Corporate CA certificate goes here.
#
# If your office Wi-Fi intercepts TLS (FortiGate SSL inspection), paste the
# corporate root / SSL-inspection CA certificate in PEM form below (the whole
# block, from its BEGIN line to its END line) and rebuild. It is added to the
# app's trust store so the ngrok HTTPS backend validates on corp Wi-Fi.
#
# Ask IT / your FortiGate admin for it — on this project the required CA was
# "CN=FG6H1FTB22904052, O=Fortinet" (the dev machine only had an unrelated
# "CN=support" Fortinet root, which does NOT validate the intercepted certs).
#
# Until a real certificate is pasted here, this file is ignored and TLS keeps
# full verification. Meanwhile, on corp Wi-Fi use the in-app "Backend URL"
# setting to point at the laptop over plain HTTP, e.g.
#   http://192.168.137.1:8000/api
